    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                "word": "pedicle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "df442c3e-f007-46fe-9c6c-853cdaf24059",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pedicles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "446843b0-a746-36a3-86a8-57a928af9fd0",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fleshy line used to attach and anchor brachiopods and some bivalve molluscs to a substrate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "565f574c-824b-4f23-9b8b-66cf42d74bab",
                                "sense_id": "446843b0-a746-36a3-86a8-57a928af9fd0",
                                "text": "A species of shell-fish, often found sticking by its pedicle to the bottom of ships, doing no other injury than deadening the way a little: \"Barnacles, termed soland geese In th' islands of the Orcades.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f034ff4e-27fa-3a56-b1cf-e1ed199a7a70",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The attachment point for antlers in cervids."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1efca9e-f6f2-4c85-9eb9-2b7dc4fb7b46",
                                "sense_id": "f034ff4e-27fa-3a56-b1cf-e1ed199a7a70",
                                "text": "His long, rakish horns are mounted on a pedicle that extends above his head, thus accentuating the droll length of his features."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db39761e-0436-31bf-8588-dbb23779b06a",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A stalk that attaches a tumour to normal tissue"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46bd1f10-ef5c-4355-80a2-196ca75f0b94",
                                "sense_id": "db39761e-0436-31bf-8588-dbb23779b06a",
                                "text": "--Figure 3. Fig. 4, Plate 58, represents the neck of the bladder and neighbouring part of the urethra of an ox, in which a polypous growth is seen attached by a long pedicle to the veru montanum and blocking up the neck of the bladder."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba63744b-85bf-4cfe-b71f-12e784d3ff81",
                                "sense_id": "db39761e-0436-31bf-8588-dbb23779b06a",
                                "text": "One of these women, a secundipara, had gone two weeks over time, and had a large ovarian cyst, the pedicle of which had become twisted, the fluid in the cyst being sanguineous."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a3ed423-aef1-3c70-81fe-095754dad801",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "pedicel (any sense)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3d4ba48-ca36-44dc-89ab-117e93e1654e",
                                "sense_id": "2a3ed423-aef1-3c70-81fe-095754dad801",
                                "text": "One of the ends is lengthened out into a neck or pedicle, which is as long as the egg proper."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "086a4de3-a525-39d9-a2e2-a8a766c43b43",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "peduncle (any sense)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8aa2d8b-fa94-461f-9994-126ac77864f9",
                                "sense_id": "086a4de3-a525-39d9-a2e2-a8a766c43b43",
                                "text": "The chimpanzee Heschl's gyrus homolog also showed evidence of a strongly excavated middle Heschl's sulcus, within the confines of a single gyral pedicle, predominantly in the right hemisphere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea553268-1777-4677-a789-544871c5ba23",
                                "sense_id": "086a4de3-a525-39d9-a2e2-a8a766c43b43",
                                "text": "The surface of the extracellular space at the base of the cone pedicle in goldfish has been estimated to be between 0.01 to 0.1 µm 2 depending on the fixation procedure used [ C. A. V. Vandenbranden, et al., Vision Res."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c261117b-546d-3470-b81f-70ae357396d7",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Part of a skin or tissue graft temporarily left attached to its original site."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "932029a2-2467-3e9e-8405-bb7fa057c58d",
                        "entry_id": "3b28186c-4da0-3ce9-ba90-540aa72fc66a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fetter for the foot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
